@mcollina is that the appropriate solution to this issue? The way I read it, they would just like to supply a config option that says "register these content types to the default parser as well." Something like:

```js
const fastify = require('fastify')({
  extraDefaultContentTypes: ['text/json']
})
```

If we are going to expose the default parser so that anyone can register it as many times as they like on their own, then I wonder if the better approach is to create a new plugin as a separate module. Then we depend on that module in core.
